A||||21||87PegasusGT||Turbo 3.4 DOHC||||1||
Z||000000||87PegasusGT||03-21-2000||04:23 PM||||Anyone know if this has been done? I just finished a book on turbo designing and reached the conclusion that twin turbos aren't necessarily the way to go in my application. If the Northstar can be turboed, can't the 3.4 DTC? It should give you roughly 300hp  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||03-21-2000||04:37 PM||||The shop that works on my car also built and maintains the worlds ONLY Twin Turbo CRX. if you can force feed a 1.8 liter honda motor 27psi you surely can cram that into a 3.4 DOHC. James (shop owner) has been bugin me to get twin T25s for my 2.8. theres plenty of roon and since i don't have A/C i can use the old A/C line hooks to hold the coolant lines for the intercooler. 300hp is nothing. A mild build and 15psi on a basicly stock 2.8 with proper fuel managment will yeild those numbers.. I've opted for a supercharger. Less fabrication and still pulls an easy 14psi.. I'll probly never run that much but I could if i wanted too. Twin small turbos will give you the volume you need and pressure you want with less lag, on a medium size (T03-04/ TD-05, Super 16G)  will give you CRAZY mid and upper RPM #s, but won't have the botom end. What kind of engine managment system are you looking at? Hal-TEC, Accel, Link, Eletromotive, just courious. as for you question. No, sorry don't know if it has been done but it's not that difficult.   oh shop page... <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||william_thorniii||03-21-2000||04:56 PM||||87,<P>You are talking about my dream set up.  The closest thing that I know of is a gentleman in WV running a supercharged TDC.  I am sure that somebody out there has done it.  If not one of us crazy Fiero guys, then one of those crazy W body guys or a T-Regal guy.  Please keep me updated on your quest.  I have every intention of either a Turbo TDC or a Northstar in my project vehicle.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
Z||000003||stimpy||03-21-2000||07:17 PM||||I have met the man who has done this and can do it again and again. (How fat is your wallet?) The man is...(drumroll) CHRIS WEST  of WEST COAST FIERO!!  Chris is located in California in an unassuming shop near Venice Beach and is a perfectionist when it comes to working on Fiero conversions. Chris' personal beast is an SE with a 3.4 TDC (all chromed... oh so pretty!) with a nasty hair dryer bolted on. Be prepared to be without your car for a while, and if you want to do it right without cutting corners, be prepared to write a hefty check. Chris does not do half assed work, and he don't give it away for free.<BR>Tell him stimpy sent ya, I am tryin to get enough referrals to rate a 3.8!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  j/k!||||reg||1
Z||000004||turbo86se||03-21-2000||10:58 PM||||stimpy, I completely agree with you about <BR>Chris West. He is an excellent Fiero <BR>resource. He probably won't remember me, <BR>but I bought a set of 85GT wheels with <BR>tires for a very good price about 4 or 5 <BR>years ago. I had no computer, so he <BR>called me a couple times to tell me the <BR>tires condition and that they were <BR>shipped. When they arrived, they were <BR>spotless! I think he lived in Indiana at <BR>the time.<P>87Pegasus, removing the 2.8 from my 86SE <BR>and installing a 3.4 with my MillerWoods <BR>turbo has always been in the back of my <BR>mind. Someday I'll do it. But there's no <BR>reason to remove the mint V6 with barely <BR>over 51,000 adrenaline rushing miles. I'm <BR>running 0-60 in about 5.6 seconds, <BR>certainly faster than my buddy's Crown <BR>Victoria police cruiser that I was in for <BR>several hours last night (ride along). <BR>Fast enough for me, at least for now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||phillip||03-22-2000||01:00 AM||||i think ACE dose a tdc turbo set up too. it seemed like it was part of their site at one time.||||reg||1
Z||000006||87PegasusGT||03-22-2000||03:18 PM||||I want the exotic sound and extra horses w/o extra high cost of a DOHC setup. I know Fiero Store and Gary/s Custom Exotics both sell 190hp + 2.8/3.1 but boy are they spendy $3000+. Anyone know any cheaper sources? Because I think a strong motor that is built like this, can be turboed and I won't have to modify anything....||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||03-22-2000||04:52 PM||||Jim Clark Engines here in atlanta might be able to do it for less.. he's building a STUIPD strong 1.8 for S/C acura for less than that... jimclarkengines@aol.com  Or you can do it all yourself just gathering the parts isn't all that difficult.. his work can be seen at <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  under the acura banner... it's impressive...||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||03-22-2000||07:12 PM||||Before spending money on a big conversion, get lots of references from people who have done business with the company that you are thinking of working with.  I have heard of people being quite satisfied with ACE, and from others who were quite disapponted. Forum member Big O (my dad) has done business with both ACE and West Coast.  I believe that he would endorse Chris West.  I am sure he would be happy to relate his experiences off forum.||||reg||1
Z||000009||loafer87gt||03-23-2000||12:58 AM||||Hey guys, check out this guys page. He has mated an Eaton M62 supercharger with a 3.4 DOHC and is putting it his plastic fantastic.<BR> <A HREF="http://mae.wvu.edu/~mhawkins/super34.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://mae.wvu.edu/~mhawkins/super34.htm</A> <P>I have always wanted to do a 3.4 conversion, but I heard that they are just as bad for blowing head gaskets as the quad 4. Any truth to this? The other options I've considered are the 3.5 Shortstar and the Yamaha SHO engine. The SHO is an awesome engine, there was a guy in High Tech Performance that took one of these and supercharged it and was making almost 400 HP with a 8000 RPM redline. They are also some of the coolest looking engines I have seen. I remember in one of my old Fiero Owner magazines reading about a company that did these swaps in California, but I can't recall the name. Does anyone here know?||||reg||1
Z||000010||Dan86gt3.8||03-23-2000||01:08 AM||||Hey I'll recomend ace if you want me to, I did his 3.8 kit and am pretty satified, except I think it needs a dogbone to be  perfect.  Anywyas when I was there I saw there 3.4 tdc open road race car, and if I am correct it was a special built motor that was making "350" horses.  I am not sure if it was turbo'ed or not but it was defenitely set up for open road racing (like the ones in utah and arizona).  Anyways if you have info e-mail him, last time I was there the car was for sell, but its reall race modified, and I don't know how streetable it is.  But anywyas I am not completely positive about the specs of the car.  Well guys keep me posted, I love hearing about v6 swaps, especially when they are turbo'ed or s/c'ed!!!!!!!!!!!!!!  I almost went with the 3.4 but opted for a 3.8 since they are more readibly acessible.||||reg||1
Z||000011||batboy||03-23-2000||11:05 AM||||With the 3.4 TDC, I've heard more hard luck stories about them tearing up the timing belts and idler pulleys than anything.||||reg||1
Z||000012||JIM GOOSE||03-23-2000||11:31 AM||||Twin-turbo setups got a big BOOST from the early 80s Formula One Renault cars. A 1.5 liter V-6(DOHC 4valve) with twinturbos put out 1100-1200 hp in qualifying tune. A lot of the mfrs used the same configuration for their cars(Ferrari,BMW) due the phenomenal power output. There are motorcycles with twinturbos & intercoolers that have 3-400 hp so you can put em on almost anything if you have room. I would think you'd be short on room around the 3.4 TC due to its excessive width across the heads. I have an IFG twinturbo kit which I plan to install on my 2.8 at some point. Putting in a 3.4 and turbos is just too much complication for me to understand. Installing a turbo setup and getting your engine to run right and stay together is enough trouble.||||reg||6
Z||000013||87PegasusGT||03-23-2000||03:15 PM||||Jim;<BR>Have you already emailed me about your twin turbo setup? I have 2 other options. Twin turboing the standard  Camaro 3.4 which has a base 160hp or buying the 2.8-3.1 195hp stroker Fiero engine (NO mods to install)and slapping a turbo or 2 on THAT.. What do you guys think?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Dan86gt3.8||03-23-2000||04:27 PM||||hey guys how about a aftermarket turbo on a 3.8, I was thinking of trying to do a gn motor, but others (shaun) suggested I go with an aftermarket turbo for it.  which is a good idea I think.  With one good fat turbo on there I should have what 300 hp?  Just a thought, but when I get out of school and get a real job I want to do a 3.8 turbo or a northstar, I guess ut depends on how rich I become.......||||reg||14
